  "notes": "Compound of {合格|ごうかく} (passing, success) + する. The thing passed is marked with に: {試験|しけん}に{合格|ごうかく}する (to pass an exam).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. Takes に for the exam or target, not を.\n- {試験|しけん}に{合格|ごうかく}する: to pass an exam\n- {検査|けんさ}に{合格|ごうかく}する: to pass an inspection\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {受|う}かる: to pass (an exam) — more casual, native-Japanese verb with the same meaning\n- {通|とお}る: to get through; pass — broader, also used for screenings\n- {落|お}ちる: to fail — the antonym",
